# amont-agent-cases-v1
# Reviewed judgements for this rule. Generated by
#   amont-agent explain <rule> --format cases
# then labelled by hand. `amont-agent corpus check` replays every line through
# the rules as they stand today, and runs as a test — so widening a rule in a
# way that breaks a judgement somebody already made is a red build.
#
# match   the rule SHOULD fire here
# nomatch the rule must stay silent here — these are the ones that matter,
#         because a corpus of positives alone measures recall, not precision
# ?       nobody has looked yet; never counts as evidence
#
# This rule is answered from the Read tool's payload and a stat of the file,
# never from a command string, so `examine` never fires and every shell line
# here is a negative: shell reads that `whole-file-dump` owns, not this rule.
#
# A `Read <window> <bytes> <agent> <path>` line is a Read call, judged by the
# same decision the hook makes (`read_unbounded_large::decide`) on a regular
# file of that size. The matches are the 2026-11-09 replay sample (seed
# 20261109, window 2026-10-23..11-06): first whole reads by a non-reviewer
# agent, sizes as observed, paths repo-relative. The negatives are the
# reviewer reads from that replay (their size set past the threshold, since
# the exemption is what is judged) and one case per path exemption, window
# and the exact threshold.

nomatch	cat src/hook.rs
nomatch	sed -n 1,400p src/hook.rs
nomatch	head -c 20000 big.log
nomatch	grep -n 'fn on_file' src/hook.rs
